cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Zeitgeber, please cite it as below."
title: "Zeitgeber: a body-clock planner for night-shift workers"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Panes
    given-names: Lawrence
    website: "https://lauurnce.is-a.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lauurnce/zeitgeber"
url: "https://zeitgeber-web.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Zeitgeber turns a weekly shift schedule into a 14-day light profile, simulates
  the human circadian clock with published models (Forger 1999, Jewett 1999,
  Hannay 2019) through the open-source circadian package, scores misalignment
  between the clock and the schedule, and searches for a plan of light, sleep,
  nap and caffeine timing within published shift-work rules. A wellness tool,
  not medical advice.
keywords:
  - circadian rhythm
  - chronobiology
  - shift work
  - sleep
  - BPO
  - Philippines
